w: Ah, ho- ly Je- sus, how hast Thou of- fend- ed, That man to judge Thee hath in hate pre- tend- ed?
w: Who was the guil- ty? Who brought this up- on Thee? A- las, my trea- son, Je- sus, hath un- done Thee.
w: Lo, the Good Shep- herd for the sheep is of- fered; The slave hath sinned, and the Son hath suf- fer- ed;
w: For me, kind Je- sus, was Thy in- car- na- tion, Thy mor- tal sor- row, and Thy life's o- bla- tion;
w: There- fore, kind Je- sus, since I can- not pay Thee, I do ad- ore Thee, and will ev- er pray Thee,
