w: By foes de- rid- ed, by Thine own re- ject- ed, O most af- flict- ed.
w: ’Twas I, Lord, Je- sus, I it was de- nied Thee! I cru- ci- fied Thee.
w: For man's a- tone- ment, while he no- thing hee- deth, God in- ter- ced- eth.
w: Thy death of ang- uish and Thy bit- ter pas- sion, For my sal- va- tion.
w: Think on Thy pi- ty and Thy love un- swerv- ing, Not my de- serv- ing.
